From d147907cd2fe1869747ea70e536f04f0d09ef2e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:20:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Draw the extensions toolbar into the captured toolbar bitmap

While the browser controls animate, what is on screen is not the live toolbar
but a bitmap the compositor holds. ToolbarViewResourceAdapter.onCaptureStart
puts ToolbarPhone into texture capture mode, dispatchDraw then takes the
drawWithoutBackground branch, and that method paints an explicit list of
children: home, back, the location bar, the optional button, signin, the tab
stack button and the menu.

There is no entry for the extensions container, because upstream only ever has
one on tablets and ToolbarTablet has no equivalent capture path. Patch 0003 put
that container in toolbar_phone.xml, so on a phone the captured bitmap carried
every other button and an empty gap where the extension icons belong. Scrolling
the toolbar out of view and back showed the toolbar returning complete except
for the extensions, which arrived only once the live view took over.

The icons were never missing from the view tree. Their views, child count,
drawables, alpha, dimensions and attachment state are all correct throughout;
only the capture omitted them, which is why nothing at the Java view layer
explained it.

Drawn in layout order, between the signin button and the tab stack button, and
guarded on visibility and non-zero width like the optional button above it, for
the reason that guard already documents.
---
 .../browser/toolbar/top/ToolbarPhone.java      | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/android/toolbar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/toolbar/top/ToolbarPhone.java b/chrome/browser/ui/android/toolbar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/toolbar/top/ToolbarPhone.java
index efb5b0b4bb3..8e38c6764d2 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/android/toolbar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/toolbar/top/ToolbarPhone.java
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/android/toolbar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/toolbar/top/ToolbarPhone.java
@@ -1697,6 +1697,24 @@ public class ToolbarPhone extends ToolbarLayout
             }
         }
 
+        // Draw the extensions toolbar. This method paints an explicit list of children
+        // into the bitmap the compositor shows while the browser controls animate, and
+        // upstream's list has no entry for the extensions container because upstream only
+        // has one on tablets. Patch 0003 put that container in toolbar_phone.xml, so
+        // without this the captured toolbar carries every other button and an empty gap
+        // where the extension icons belong. Visibility and width are checked for the same
+        // reason as the optional button above.
+        View extensionsContainer =
+                mToolbarButtonsContainer.findViewById(R.id.extensions_toolbar_container);
+        if (extensionsContainer != null
+                && extensionsContainer.getVisibility() == View.VISIBLE
+                && extensionsContainer.getWidth() != 0) {
+            canvas.save();
+            ViewUtils.translateCanvasToView(mToolbarButtonsContainer, extensionsContainer, canvas);
+            extensionsContainer.draw(canvas);
+            canvas.restore();
+        }
+
         // Draw the tab stack button and associated text if necessary.
         ToggleTabStackButtonCoordinator tabSwitcherButtonCoordinator =
                 getTabSwitcherButtonCoordinator();
